## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate onboarding into concrete artifacts, rituals, and measurable outcomes for a distributed setting.

## Key Concepts
- Onboarding playbooks that scale across time zones
- Clear artifacts and acceptance criteria
- Lightweight rituals that sustain momentum
- Quantifiable ramp metrics and experiments

## Code Example
```javascript
function rampScore({timeToFirstCommit, issuesClosed, prMergeTime}) {
  const t = timeToFirstCommit <= 7 ? 1 : 0;
  const i = issuesClosed >= 5 ? 1 : 0;
  const p = prMergeTime <= 48 ? 1 : 0;
  return t + i + p;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate onboarding checklists and artifact generation?
- How would you adapt artifacts for contractors vs. full-time engineers?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates how a manager translates reliability goals into a concrete plan, balancing speed and risk, across teams and regions.

## Key Concepts
- SLOs and SLIs for latency and errors
- Incident response and runbooks
- Canary deployments and feature flags
- Tail latency and multi-region observability
- Instrumentation, profiling, and postmortems

## Code Example
```javascript
function percentile(arr, p){
  if (arr.length===0) return 0;
  const s = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.floor((p/100)*(s.length-1));
  return s[idx];
}
```

